    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/dth-sc/v0/ns/glossary/dth-sc/traceability",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/dth-sc/v0/ns/glossary/dth-sc"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Traceability"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The ability to trace something. In some cases, it is interpreted as the ability to verify the history, location or application of an item by means of documented identification."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "Handbook definition, quoted. Open: not adopted, nothing chosen between alternatives. The handbook gives a second definition in Chapter 4 (PDF 54), citing GS1: the ability 'to see the movement of health products across the supply chain'. Both are kept as alternatives; neither is chosen (litlfred/smart-ra#140). dth-pc and dth-sfp link to this term.",
